    "body":  "Closes #820\n\n## What this changes\n\nAdds the Sentry connector to Switch\u0027s service connection catalog under `core/switch_core/connections/catalog/sentry/`, allowing agents to inspect Sentry issues, events, stack traces, and releases through Sentry\u0027s remote MCP server at `https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp`.\n\n### Why `adapter: api_key`\n\nIssue #820 specifies preferring OAuth with Dynamic Client Registration (DCR) where available, then a static OAuth app, then a key, and explaining the choice in the PR:\n\n1. While `mcp.sentry.dev` advertises OAuth with DCR, it does not provide an RFC 7662 token introspection endpoint or an OIDC `/userinfo` REST endpoint to query identity.\n2. Upstream `https://sentry.io/api/0/users/me/` rejects downstream worker OAuth tokens with HTTP 401.\n3. Sentry User Auth Tokens are validated directly against `GET https://sentry.io/api/0/users/me/` (`account_id: id`, `label: email`).\n4. Sentry MCP natively supports Sentry User Auth Tokens via the `Authorization: Sentry-Bearer {auth_token}` header.\n5. This matches Switch\u0027s `adapter: api_key` architecture (following the same design as Datadog).\n\n### Included changes\n\n- Added catalog definition `core/switch_core/connections/catalog/sentry/connection.yaml`.\n- Added agent skill `core/switch_core/connections/catalog/sentry/skill/SKILL.md` detailing scoped queries, inspecting errors before mutating issues, and data privacy with zero credential references.\n- Added vendored Sentry mark at `console/apps/switch-console-desktop/src/assets/images/connections/sentry.svg`.\n- Added attribution notice to `console/apps/switch-console-desktop/src/assets/images/connections/NOTICE.md`.\n- Registered brand color in `console/apps/switch-console-desktop/src/renderer/features/switch-servers/connection-icon.tsx`.\n- Added Sentry to `console/packages/agent-providers/src/host/service-notices.ts`.\n- Added catalog loader unit tests in `core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_loader.py` and registry tests in `core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_registry.py`.\n\n## How it was tested\n\n- Ran catalog loader unit tests:\n  ```bash\n  uv run pytest core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_loader.py -v\n  ```\n  Result: 128 passed.\n- Ran registry tests:\n  ```bash\n  uv run pytest core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_registry.py -k \"test_a_key_service\" -v\n  ```\n  Result: passed.\n- Ran code style and lint checks:\n  ```bash\n  uv run ruff check core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_loader.py core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_registry.py\n  uv run ruff format --check core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_loader.py core/tests/switch_core/connections/test_registry.py\n  ```\n  Result: all passed.",
